SpeakCraft — Complete Learning Experience, Dashboard, Personalization & Vocabulary Builder Upgrade

Project Context

You are working on SpeakCraft, an existing native Android English communication learning application.

Existing technology

* Kotlin
* Jetpack Compose
* Material 3
* Firebase Authentication
* Cloud Firestore
* Android SpeechRecognizer / offline speech recognition
* Android Text-to-Speech
* MediaPipe (where supported)
* Local Intelligence Orchestrator
* Local Evaluation Engine
* Audio DSP and speech analysis
* Lightweight on-device models

The application already has learning activities, learning paths, evaluation strategies, vocabulary and speaking exercises.

First inspect the existing repository, architecture, screens, database models, navigation, repositories, ViewModels and documentation.

Do not rebuild the application from scratch. Extend the existing architecture and reuse working components.

CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE REQUIREMENTS

1. Android-native Kotlin and Jetpack Compose only.
2. No React, Electron, web application or unnecessary backend rewrite.
3. Do not introduce large language models.
4. Do not introduce paid cloud AI dependencies.
5. All core learning, vocabulary evaluation, scoring and feedback must work offline.
6. Firebase Authentication and Firestore can continue supporting account management and progress synchronization.
7. Do not send personal recordings, audio, video or transcripts to cloud AI.
8. Preserve existing learning activities and user progress.
9. All UI must support small, medium and large Android screens.
10. Follow MVVM, repository pattern, modular architecture and existing project conventions.

